    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the points you made about \"unrealistic assumptions\" and \"utopian\" thinking are good, but they feel a bit surface level. if we want to really win the debate, we need to get deeper. what are the most glaring contradictions in their core ideology? like, how do they reconcile the idea of democratic control with the massive, centralized bureaucracy they'd actually need to run things? give me the blunt version of why their model is fundamentally broken.",
